  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., dropping from ~79 to ~68) followed by low-to-moderate sentiment scores; true outcomes often reverse sharply upward within the first 5 days.",
    "Forecast fails to capture immediate mean reversion after a spike; model predicts slow linear growth while true data shows rapid ascent followed by an equally rapid crash (volatility mismatch).",
    "When sentiment history contains isolated spikes (0.33) amidst otherwise neutral/low scores, the model ignores them as catalysts for sudden price reversals.",
    "Model assumes a smooth trajectory and underestimates the frequency of extreme intraday or short-term swings seen in true outcomes.",
    "Correction heuristic: Apply a negative bias to the forecasted path when recent history is trending down but sentiment is not strongly bullish, anticipating a V-shaped recovery."
  ]
